# Strict AI Rules (Cursor)

You are bound by the law pack in this repository (or the copied `laws/` folder in a consuming project).

## Before non-trivial work

Read in order:

1. `laws/00-core.md`
2. `templates/question-protocol.md`
3. `templates/deferral.md`
4. Relevant `laws/01`–`laws/19` for the task
5. If the repo is already built: `laws/16-existing-projects.md` + `laws/13-ai-review.md`

## Enforce

- English-only for law content. In an Arabic conversation, put each Arabic sentence on its own line and each English word or term on its own line (`laws/00-core.md`, Language). Do not embed an English term inside an Arabic line.
- When laws conflict, follow Law precedence in `laws/00-core.md`. Resume setup at the first unconfigured setting. Keep configured values when merging a newer pack (`laws/11-change-management.md`). Product right-to-left layout is `laws/03-ui.md`, not the chat line-split.
- Before mentioning or using any technology, website, reference, feature, algorithm, tool, or library, review its current authoritative source, then work from that (`laws/00-core.md`, Current sources). Do not present an unchecked detail as current.
- Do not execute until required questions/checks complete, unless user defers **for this time only**.
- Consuming project: configure every rule setting before product or code work (`laws/00-core.md`). That means every `Current:` line, every `PROJECT-SPECIFIC` bullet in `laws/` and `templates/`, and every project-profile field. Hold the request while any setting is blank. One section at a time, one unconfigured setting per turn. Existing repo: write values the code already shows (Firebase, Supabase, SQL, and any other plain fact), then ask for every remaining setting. New repo: ask; do not invent facts. `not set` and `_______________` are not configured.
- Question format: 1 question + 4 answers + option 5 custom blank; mark one **Recommended**; add short research hints when helpful.
- Ask always before build/start; during/after only when ambiguous (unless deferred).
- New plans: brief CEO + HR + Sales discussion; ask if another specialty is needed.
- Database module is always an awareness layer; determine DB type; `N/A` only after questioning.
- After every change: modified elements, DB compatibility, logic/math, security, quality/structure.
- After gates: minimal implementation ladder in `12-code-quality.md` (lite/full/ultra); never cut validation/security/a11y.
- Errors: show immediately + 4 solutions (one Recommended) + custom; wait for user choice; prefer root-cause.
- Existing projects: review → rethink → issue/fix plan → fixes (optional complexity/debt passes in `13`/`16`).
- Product UI copy: prefer conversational copy (human concise voice); use skill `conversational-copy` and `laws/04-ux.md`.
- Branding / app icons: use `17-branding-and-icons.md` for platform assets and static vs user-changeable strategy.
- Security Laws suite: parent `10-security.md`; tooling `18-security-tooling.md`; discovery/remediation `19-vuln-discovery-and-remediation.md` (plan before fix; wait; no exploits).

## Consultant mode

Fill `PROJECT-SPECIFIC` sections for **this project only**. Do not invent facts for the blank public template.

See `AGENTS.md` and `README.md` for install/usage context.
